# Mosquitto access control list (ACL): the planned rules (architecture §5, §12).
#
# NOT ACTIVE. The broker has no acl_file today, so every user with a password may
# publish and subscribe to every topic. Turning this on is a later, separate step
# (mosquitto/README.md, "Tightening the broker"): create the users first, then add
#   acl_file /etc/mosquitto/acl
# to conf.d/local.conf and restart Mosquitto. Users not listed here get no access.
#
# One user per device and per service. Device users are named after the hub
# (<location>00); topics use the location. Replace ADMIN_USER with the real admin
# username on the server (it is a personal name, so it is not in git).

# --- Administrator: debugging with mosquitto_sub / mosquitto_pub -------------------
user ADMIN_USER
topic readwrite #
topic read $SYS/#

# --- Services ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# mqtt2sqlite and mqtt2slack: read only
user telemetry
topic read sensor/#
topic read telemetry/#
topic read event/#
topic read config/#
topic read homeassistant/device/+/config

# Control service (later, with garagebot): the only user that sends commands and
# settings, and the only one that may remove a device's discovery message.
user control
topic read sensor/#
topic read event/#
topic read config/#
topic read homeassistant/device/+/config
topic write cmd/#
topic write set/#
topic write homeassistant/device/+/config

# --- Devices: each publishes only its own topics and reads only its own commands ---

# esp32-door
user backyard00
topic write sensor/backyard/#
topic write telemetry/backyard/#
topic write event/backyard/#
topic write config/backyard
topic write homeassistant/device/backyard00/config
topic read cmd/backyard/#
topic read set/backyard/#

# esp32-shed (formerly esp32-monitor)
user shed00
topic write sensor/shed/#
topic write telemetry/shed/#
topic write event/shed/#
topic write config/shed
topic write homeassistant/device/shed00/config
topic read cmd/shed/#
topic read set/shed/#

# esp32-garage
user garage00
topic write sensor/garage/#
topic write telemetry/garage/#
topic write event/garage/#
topic write config/garage
topic write homeassistant/device/garage00/config
topic read cmd/garage/#
topic read set/garage/#
